// Termination oracle: same ordering fact as compare_secret_to_input, but the
// leak is "hang vs return 0" instead of "return 1 vs 0". Often passes checkers
// that are termination-insensitive (or only care about explicit flows to return).
//
// Python driver treats subprocess TIMEOUT as secret < input, and a finished run
// with failure/success as secret >= input (same binary-search update as implicit).
int main(int input, int secret)
{
    while (secret < input) {
        int spin = 1;
    }
    return 0;
}
